(7099874, 1081474, 100393, '<td valign="top">This image has caused me to stop and pay attention. That means it is in my 7-10 voting band. (Voted earlier) <br/> <br/>Additionally, it is highly interesting/eclectic meaning it keeps me here long enough to offer a longer comment and a vote of 8 or more. <br/> <br/>This is one of my 8s - I like it. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me:<br/> <br/>1. I normally like stuff that has more story than a straight landscape can offer, but this is stunning in so many areas; it''s a lesson in/as an image.<br/> <br/>2. Stunning composition - not just structurally but in its placement of colour too.<br/> <br/>3. What wonderful light you have captured - that peak - marvellous.<br/> <br/>4. The rendering of the grass and moss, glowing - not sharp and crunchy as many make the mistake of doing.<br/> <br/>5. Paintingesque while being photographically pure.<br/> <br/>Overall, a masterclass.</td>', 'This image has caused me to stop and pay attention. That means it is in my 7-10 voting band. (Voted earlier)  Additionally, it is highly interesting/eclectic meaning it keeps me here long enough to offer a longer comment and a vote of 8 or more.  This is one of my 8s - I like it. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me: 1. I normally like stuff that has more story than a straight landscape can offer, but this is stunning in so many areas; it''s a lesson in/as an image. 2. Stunning composition - not just structurally but in its placement of colour too. 3. What wonderful light you have captured - that peak - marvellous. 4. The rendering of the grass and moss, glowing - not sharp and crunchy as many make the mistake of doing. 5. Paintingesque while being photographically pure. Overall, a masterclass.', '2013-09-07 11:16:54.000000', NULL, 1),
